  "helpFormatCoverageTitle": "2a. Format limits on origin evidence",
  "helpFormatCoverage": "**An important limit: only .docx, .odt and legacy .doc carry an editing record.**\n\n| Source | Editing record |\n|---|---|\n| .docx / .odt | ✅ yes |\n| .pdf | ❌ the format holds no editing history at all |\n| .doc (legacy) | ✅ yes (OLE2 SummaryInformation) |\n| .txt / .md | ❌ no container |\n| Image OCR | ❌ only pixels remain |\n| Pasted text | ❌ no file at all |\n\nThis bears directly on pillar 3: **only documents carrying an editing record are added automatically to the statistically guaranteed baseline.** If everything you receive is PDF, that baseline will never grow — you will only accumulate reference-only samples that carry no guarantee.\n\nTo make origin evidence and automatic calibration actually work, collect .docx or .odt originals rather than printed or exported PDFs. That is a workflow requirement, not something the software can work around: PDF is an output format and simply does not record how the text came to be written.",
